    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n76460" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πάγ-κοινος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>common to all</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νοσήματα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
				</span></i>
			<i>Aër.</i><i><span class="en">
				2
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				17(1).2
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. σοφισταί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Poll.
					4.43
				</span></i>
			: mostly poet., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. χώρα</span>, of
			Olympia, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>O.</u>
				6.63
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παγκοίνοις . . Δηοῦς ἐν
			κόλποις</span>, of Eleusis, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ant.</u>
				1120
			</span></i> (lyr.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πληγεὶς θεοῦ μάστιγι
				παγκοίνῳ</span>, i.e. by death, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Th.</u>
				608
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξ Ἅιδου παγκοίνου λίμνας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>El.</u>
					138
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἓν ἀπέχθημα π.
			βροτοῖς</span> one object of hate <i>common to all</i>
			mankind, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Tr.</u>
				425
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. τέρας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>Pae.</u>
					9.10
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στάσις π.</span>
			<i>all</i> the band <i>together</i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ch.</u>
				458
			</span></i> (lyr.). Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-νως</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Man.
					4.506
				</span></i>
			.</div>
